.TH ASTERCTL 1 "2026-09-28" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl \- introspect and control Aster nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RB ( \-\-token
.I TOKEN
|
.B \-\-token\-file
.IR PATH )
.RI [ COMMAND
.RI [ COMMAND-OPTIONS ]]
.YS
.SY asterctl
.B \-\-help
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl
is a command-line utility for introspecting and controlling Aster nodes.
It communicates with a running
.B aster-agent
over RPC.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Display node status. Default, if no command provided.
.TP
.B publish
Publish an Event. See
.BR asterctl-publish (1)
.TP
.B query
Query stored Events. See
.BR asterctl-query (1)
.TP
.BI subscribe " TOPIC"
Create a persistent Event subscription and print its ID. See
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1)
.TP
.B subscriptions
List Event subscriptions. See
.BR asterctl-subscriptions (1)
.TP
.BI unsubscribe " SUBSCRIPTION_ID"
Remove an Event subscription. See
.BR asterctl-unsubscribe (1)
.SH OPTION SYNTAX
Long options with values accept both
.B \-\-name value
and
.BR \-\-name=value .
Short options with values require a separate argument, for example
.BR "\-p 8181" .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
When supported by the command, print the response in JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " "\-\-host IP"
Connect to the agent at the specified loopback IPv4 or IPv6 address.
Non-loopback addresses are rejected because RPC uses plaintext HTTP.
Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " "\-\-port PORT"
Connect to the specified RPC port.
Default: 8181.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Set the client timeout for each RPC to an integer from 1 to 86400 seconds.
Default: 10 seconds. Each query page gets its own deadline.
The agent may enforce a shorter deadline; the current aster-agent caps each
RPC at 30 seconds, even when the client requests more.
This does not limit time spent reading a publication payload from stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " "\-\-token TOKEN"
Use TOKEN to authenticate with the agent.
Either this option or
.B \-\-token\-file
is required to run a command; they cannot be used together.
.IP
Command-line tokens may be visible in process listings or saved in shell
history.
Consider using
.BR \-\-token\-file .
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " PATH"
Read the API token from PATH.
Either this option or
.B \-\-token
is required to run a command; they cannot be used together.
.SH OPERATION KEYS
Both publish and subscribe require
.BR "\-\-operation\-key KEY|auto" .
Use an explicit key or auto to generate one.
For retries, use the actual key from the previous attempt and the same request.
.SH OUTPUT
Results go to stdout. 
Diagnostics go to stderr.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion, including an identical existing subscription,
a removed or already absent subscription, or help.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl-publish (1),
.BR asterctl-query (1),
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1),
.BR asterctl-subscriptions (1),
.BR asterctl-unsubscribe (1)
